    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (77.42) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against soft pitching. **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier start, leveraging a high base projection and a juicy matchup against the underwhelming Gasser; he is the cornerstone of our offensive ceiling today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also presents a high-efficiency profile, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Grant Holmes provides the necessary lift to push him well into the \"Strong\" tier. While **Andy Pages** (67.85), **Josh Jung** (64.46), and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) are also locked in with solid \"Strong\" ratings\u2014bolstered by wind-out conditions and positive park factors\u2014the focus remains on maximizing volume in categories where we face stiff competition.\n\nThe bench decision for **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77) was the most difficult pivot, as his projected output was respectable but ultimately cannibalized by the superior efficiency of our infield core. While **Nolan Schanuel** offers reliability, the optimizer preferred the high-ceiling platoon advantages presented by **Miguel Vargas** and **Dominic Smith** in their respective matchups. We continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, who remains sidelined by a rainout, and our ongoing IL concerns regarding **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. As a final note of caution, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) faces an elite challenge in the form of Skenes. His score has been suppressed by the SP\u2019s high-caliber skill set; while he remains in the UTIL slot, he represents our highest volatility risk today. We will keep a close eye on the official lineups for **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Dominic Smith** to ensure no late-breaking adjustments are required.",
